{"type": "say", "text": "Thank you, Victor, Nadia, Owen, and Priya. I'm tracking progress on all four areas of the incident authorization form. Victor has covered equipment repair — cracked manifold isolation valve seat, four-hour replacement, six isolation points documented on a lockout worksheet to be attached to the incident record. Nadia, please go ahead and share your findings on the spill volume and hazardous-waste disposal requirements — we need that for the hazardous-waste handling entry. Priya, after Nadia speaks, I'd like you to walk us through the full details of your wipe sampling results so we can document the panel disposition. Owen, once we have Priya's and Nadia's full updates, we'll finalize the production recovery numbers. Let's keep moving through this systematically."}
```

```json
{"type": "say", "text": "Understood, Elena. While Nadia prepares her update, I want to confirm on my end: the six isolation points on my lockout worksheet are all currently secured, so the booth remains safely isolated for the spill cleanup work. Once Nadia and Priya share their findings, I'll be ready to address any maintenance questions that come up — for instance, if the spill volume or panel contamination situation affects the scope of the valve replacement or requires additional isolation measures. I'll have the lockout worksheet attached to the incident record immediately after this meeting as I mentioned."}
